                                   ms.par                 
                                   ========
                               "disk.par" type
                      parameters for solar disk observations        
                              (format a8,i8)                               
                 * (character 18) parameters often modified  
                   for all parameters generally: 1 = action; 0 = inoperative 
                                                        
                                 SUCCESSIVE STEPS
                                 ================
     ixy       1 *  computation of average files dark, flat, field-stop 
   igeom       1 *  calculation geometry
  icalib       1    calculation calibration
    ibmc       0    elementary calibrated c-files (1 file per time) 
    icmd       0    d-files (spectroheliograms and I/V maps)
    ides       0    dessins   (1;   0=no plot)
  iquick       0    q-filesfor full scanned targets     
  igrayq       0    plots of q-files
                             Automatic plots during calculation
                        (0 = plots    available only afterwards with "gv")
   igeo1       1    idem  igeo1.ps  fig1
   igeo2       1    idem  igeo2.ps  fig2
   igeo3       1    idem  igeo3.ps  fig3
   igeo4       1    idem  igeo4.ps  fig4
  icalib       1    idem  calib.ps  fig5
icalplot       0    idem  cal.ps    fig6                                  
  iobsD1       0    idem  non calibrated solar observations obsD1.ps
                          divided by averages over same X-value
                          (approx. constant wavelength)
  iobsD2       1    idem  obsD2.ps with calibration
    iobs       0    idem  obs.ps for observations with calibration   
 ivprof1       1    idem  ivprof1  fig 7 degree 3
 ivprof2       1    idem  ivprof2  fig 8 degree 4
 ivprof3       1    idem  ivprof3  fig 9 degrees 3+4 
  jxpro1       0 
  jxpro2       0
  jxpro3       0
   iipro       0
   jjpro       0
 lbdvel1       5    fist width of profile for veocity measurment
                      unit=lamda between channels /10
 lbdvel2       8    second ...
 lbdvel3      10    3    (0 = no lbdvel)
  labsem       0    line emission (0) or absorption (1) for velocities
    iobs       1    idem  obs.ps for observations with calibration      
  icalwh    1200    1000 times maximum white for calN       1100
  icalbl     800    1000 times minimum black for calN               900
 iobsDwh    1200    maximum white for obsD1 (not calib.) and obsD2 (calib.)  
 iobsDbl     800    minimum black 
  iobswh    1800    maximum white for obs.ps               1800
  iobsbl     200    minimum black for obs.ps
                                                                             
   kedgx       0    pixels suppressed close to edges parallel to X
   kedgy       0       ...                                    to Y   
--------                                                                     
                                SELECTED OBSERVATIONS
                                =====================
    nfx1       1   first used dark current    1    1
    nfx2       5   last  used dark current    5    1
    nfy1       1   first used flat field      1   22
    nfy2      25    last  used flat field     25   23
    nfb1       1   first used obs
    nfb2       1   last  used obs
  nfplot       1   obs plotted and used for profiles and corrections detailed
 meanpro       1   use of mean vlues of several 4th order interpolation
    nob1       1   first image to be processed             1
    nob2       1   last  image to be processed           300  
   ntmax       5   number of images per scan
 priscan       4   = 4 for Meudon (5 images), scanning by prisms (2,3,1,5,4))  
 nobstep       5   step between first images of two scans  

     dob20170330   date of observation (optional)       
    tob100000000 * first time for observations to be processed
    tob224000000   last time              
    tdc100000000   same for dark current     
    tdc224000000           
    tfs100000000   same for field stop
    tfs224000000    
   calfs      -1   0
                   -1 if flat field Y replaces field stop Z
    tff100000000   same for flat field          109590
    tff224000000
                                  GEOMETRY
                                  ========
      is    1536    CCD X-dimension
      js    1024    CCD Y-dimension      
      li  442000    field stop length (arcsec/1000)  
      lj   61000    field stop width
   jypas   45000     < translation between images (for correlations)  
   nline       1   spectral line index                               
   ncam1       1   detector index
      nm       9   number of channels
    lbda    6563   line wavelength (Angst)
    dlbd     300   wavelength distance between channels (mA)
  ivchan   14000   velocity with channel distance (m/s)
  mupris    9000   translation between output channels (microns)
  mustep    2500   distance betwwen successive slits (microns)      
                      
   nwinp       1   number of simultaneous detectors 
   nbcln    1024   final number of X-CCD pixels        
   nblgn    1536   final number of Y-CCD pixels        
  invern       0   0   j-value of pixels of same wavelength 
                       decreases with channels
                   1   j-value of pixels of same wavelength 
                       increases with channels
     idc       1    generally 1
                    0 = dark current not subtracted 
                    -1 = dark current not abvailable
--------                                          		    
     mgx      12   minimum gradient for X lines       
     mgy      12   minimum gradient for Y-lines 
   laddx       0   lines added (on both sides) for X-lines (up and down)
   laddy       0   lines added (on both sides) for Y-lines (left and right)
     ja1     151   Y value + 1      
     ja3     851   Y value + 1      
                                                           
                                CALIBRATION
                                ===========
                    (msdp2.f: cmf1.f -> cal.ps,  bmc1.f -> fichiers c*)
  milsec     500    output pixel (unit arcsec/1000)
  icalct       0    0 = calibration by flat field
                    1 = calibration by field stop (continuum)    
  inclin       1    0 = line profiles determined by previous calculations
                        (-> jt1000,ja1000,jb1000)
                    1 = determination of mean curve of absorption line
  ncurv1       5    first channel plotted for line profile determination (4)
  ncurv2       6    last channel  .....                                  (6)
      nr       5    reference channel
  ntrans       5    reference channel for computation Ts (spectra translation)
                      if = 0, Ts deduced from profiles line centers
jaddprof       0    Points added to the mean profile profmm (left and right)
                    in addition to the profile width nm*Ts.
   x1cal     100    X value for plots of intensity calibrations
   x2cal     750    X value for plots of intensity calibrations   
   y1cal     200    first Y value for plots of intensity calibrations  
   y2cal     700    second Y value for plots of intensity calibrations  

   iedge       0    for left and right (C calibration plots)
  jparab      10  number of points from left and right for least square parab.
 leastsq       1    least squares method for tilting andle of constant lambda  
   iliss      60    smoothing over (2*iliss+1)*(2*jliss+1) points
   jliss       0    
   calbl     800    calblack*1000   for plot cal2
   calwh    1200    calwhite*1000   for plot cal2
margline       0    margin points suppressed beginning and end of i and j
                       to look for line center with profiles
   marge       0    same margin for results of calibration
   itest       1    tests for calibration computations
   jtest     121       "
   ntest       9       "
   ideg3       0    profiles with interpolationss degree 3
   ideg4       0    profiles with interpolationss degree 4
   iboth       1    profiles with interpolationss deg mixed
end                                                              
                                    